<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Southern Ming</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">until 1662</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Southern Ming were the Ming loyalist regimes that continued to resist in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> to the Qing in 1644. They were gradually defeated, with the last claimant killed in 1662. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> treat them as the last phase of the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/southern-ming.jpg" alt="Southern Ming" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Southern_Ming.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
